{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21fd7e39d99b57bc5bcd", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Permutation and Combination - Test 5", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 60, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d3f"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d3c", "title": "Mathematics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cd3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["6176f3e46581241c70729c59"], "question": {"text": "The letters of the word &#39;MANKIND&#39; are written in all possible orders and arranged in serial order as in an English dictionary. Then the serial number of the word &#39;MANKIND&#39; is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "f27a16", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cd4"}, {"id": "9b3db9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cd5"}, {"id": "aead73", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cd6"}, {"id": "0887ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cd7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cd8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["6162fc266ed13040ec8573f3"], "question": {"text": "The number of permutations, of the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn></math> without repetition, which neither contain the string <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>153</mn></math> nor the string <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2467</mn></math>, is _______ ."}, "options": [{"id": "3f84ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cd9"}, {"id": "d04d01", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cda"}, {"id": "596bd7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cdb"}, {"id": "9e4104", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cdc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cdd", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b44e9"], "question": {"text": "The total number of two digit numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>'</mo></math>, such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>7</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math> is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> , is ___ ."}, "options": [{"id": "195604", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cde"}, {"id": "32e6a2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cdf"}, {"id": "23d39c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce0"}, {"id": "32828a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["6162fc286ed13040ec857506"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of ways of giving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> distinct oranges to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> children such that each child gets at least one orange is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "21e0ce", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce3"}, {"id": "1d0ba7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce4"}, {"id": "01765b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce5"}, {"id": "27cf88", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["60e5671b499d1e49588f87fb"], "question": {"text": "The number of natural numbers, between 212 and 999 , such that the sum of their digits is 15 , is"}, "options": [{"id": "a91087", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce8"}, {"id": "388192", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ce9"}, {"id": "24fdbf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cea"}, {"id": "6947ea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ceb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cec", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54ae"], "question": {"text": "The total number of words (with or without meaning) that can be formed out of the letters of the word \"DISTRIBUTION\" taken four at a time, is equal to ______."}, "options": [{"id": "fa6b87", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236ced"}, {"id": "950261", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cee"}, {"id": "24236b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cef"}, {"id": "09da72", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2fafa66f9ce3f243b4946"], "question": {"text": "The total number of numbers, lying between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn></math> that can be formed with the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math> if the repetition of digits is not allowed and numbers are divisible by either <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "8a323c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf2"}, {"id": "81f54f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf3"}, {"id": "e13a7d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf4"}, {"id": "91a07c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "In an examination, there are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> multiple choice questions with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> choices, out of which exactly one is correct. There are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> marks for each correct answer, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;marks for each wrong answer and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> mark if the question is not attempted. Then, the number of ways a student appearing in the examination gets&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> marks is _____"}, "options": [{"id": "c59048", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf7"}, {"id": "c7c6f5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf8"}, {"id": "c0825d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cf9"}, {"id": "1da339", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cfa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cfb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d33"], "question": {"text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-element permutation with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>j</mi></math>, such that either <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are consecutive integers or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are consecutive integers.&nbsp;Then the number of such permutations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is equal to ______.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "af789e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cfc"}, {"id": "720504", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cfd"}, {"id": "233a77", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cfe"}, {"id": "95011f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236cff"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d00", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2fbbf66f9ce3f243b54a1"], "question": {"text": "The sum of all the elements in the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>&#8739;</mo></math> H.C.F. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2040</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>}&nbsp;is equal to __________."}, "options": [{"id": "f85ae9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d01"}, {"id": "c7ed0c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d02"}, {"id": "3b52da", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d03"}, {"id": "10c4ba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d04"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d05", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["60e5671b499d1e49588f87fb"], "question": {"text": "A test consists of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> multiple choice questions, each having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> alternative answers of which only one is correct. The number of ways, in which a candidate answers all six questions such that exactly four of the answers are correct, is ___________"}, "options": [{"id": "e9f2c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d06"}, {"id": "9e3fab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d07"}, {"id": "3da908", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d08"}, {"id": "c33f32", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d09"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d0a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "Number of integral solutions to the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, is equal to _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "ebe433", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d0b"}, {"id": "a48b4d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d0c"}, {"id": "a3c47a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d0d"}, {"id": "deb5d1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d0e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d0f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["6176f3e46581241c70729c59"], "question": {"text": "Let m and $\\mathrm{n},(\\mathrm{m} \\lt \\mathrm{n})$ be two 2-digit numbers. Then the total numbers of pairs $(m, n)$, such that $\\operatorname{gcd}(m, n)=6$, is ________"}, "options": [{"id": "d22828", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d10"}, {"id": "2b559b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d11"}, {"id": "9456e8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d12"}, {"id": "376b6a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d13"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d14", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54ae"], "question": {"text": "There are 4 men and 5 women in Group A, and 5 men and 4 women in Group B. If 4 persons are selected from each group, then the number of ways of selecting 4 men and 4 women is _____"}, "options": [{"id": "e588f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d15"}, {"id": "9e64ae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d16"}, {"id": "d67493", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d17"}, {"id": "94a936", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d18"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d19", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["6162fc266ed13040ec8573f3"], "question": {"text": "The number of words, with or without meaning, that can be formed using all the letters of the word ASSASSINATION so that the vowels occur together, is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "2b5edb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d1a"}, {"id": "4523f5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d1b"}, {"id": "9dd58e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d1c"}, {"id": "58f832", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d1d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d1e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "The number of ways,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math> identical cubes, of which&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> are blue and rest are red, can be placed in a row so that between any two red cubes there should be at least&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> blue cubes, is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "34208b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d1f"}, {"id": "335ae2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d20"}, {"id": "3c4560", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d21"}, {"id": "c79dea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d22"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d23", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2fafa66f9ce3f243b4946"], "question": {"text": "If the digits are not allowed to repeat in any number formed by using the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the number of all numbers greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn></math>&nbsp;is equal to __________."}, "options": [{"id": "72ed96", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d24"}, {"id": "759ab9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d25"}, {"id": "319d0e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d26"}, {"id": "5b8b45", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d27"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d28", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b44e9"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. The number of non-empty subsets of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> that have the sum of all elements a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>, is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "cf9a60", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d29"}, {"id": "0ac013", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d2a"}, {"id": "e028de", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d2b"}, {"id": "cf9fc2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d2c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d2d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["60e5671b499d1e49588f87fb"], "question": {"text": "If the letters of the word <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><msup><mi>MOTHER</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math> be permuted and all the words so formed (with or without meaning) be listed as in a dictionary, then the position of the word <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow/><mo>'</mo></msup><msup><mi>MOTHER</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math> is....."}, "options": [{"id": "5899c6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d2e"}, {"id": "35ba1b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d2f"}, {"id": "de06f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d30"}, {"id": "8ff0e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d31"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d32", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of seven digit positive integers formed using the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;only and sum of the digits equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math> is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "082547", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d33"}, {"id": "84cd68", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d34"}, {"id": "1ad0b8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d35"}, {"id": "9c0fac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f162ee0e063d9236d36"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39